      "hints": [
        "Expand $\\cos\\theta(7\\tan\\theta - 5\\cos\\theta) = 1$ using $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$.",
        "Simplify the first term to $7\\sin\\theta$ and replace $\\cos^2\\theta$ with $1 - \\sin^2\\theta$.",
        "Rearrange all terms onto one side into standard quadratic form $a\\sin^2\\theta + b\\sin\\theta + c = 0$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Expand the left-hand side of $\\cos\\theta(7\\tan\\theta - 5\\cos\\theta) = 1$ using $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$:\n$$\\cos\\theta\\left( 7\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} - 5\\cos\\theta \\right) = 7\\sin\\theta - 5\\cos^2\\theta = 1$$",
        "Substitute $\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta$ using the Pythagorean identity:\n$$7\\sin\\theta - 5(1 - \\sin^2\\theta) = 1 \\implies 7\\sin\\theta - 5 + 5\\sin^2\\theta = 1$$",
        "Rearrange into quadratic form with integer coefficients:\n$$5\\sin^2\\theta + 7\\sin\\theta - 6 = 0$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Trigonometric Identities": "Uses $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ to get $7\\sin\\theta - 5\\cos^2\\theta = 1$ (M1). Applies $\\cos^2\\theta = 1-\\sin^2\\theta$ (M1). Obtains $5\\sin^2\\theta + 7\\sin\\theta - 6 = 0$ (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
