      "hints": [
        "Use the quadratic from part (a) with argument $2x$: $5\\sin^2(2x) + 7\\sin(2x) - 6 = 0$.",
        "Factorise to find $\\sin(2x) = \\frac{3}{5}$, rejecting $\\sin(2x) = -2$.",
        "Find all angles for $2x$ in the interval $0^\\circ < 2x < 360^\\circ$ and divide each by 2."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Apply the identity from part (a) with $\\theta = 2x$:\n$$5\\sin^2(2x) + 7\\sin(2x) - 6 = 0$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic in $\\sin(2x)$:\n$$(5\\sin(2x) - 3)(\\sin(2x) + 2) = 0$$\n$$\\sin(2x) = \\frac{3}{5} = 0.6 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\sin(2x) = -2 \\quad (\\text{reject since } -2 < -1)$$",
        "Solve $\\sin(2x) = 0.6$ for $0^\\circ < 2x < 360^\\circ$ (given $0^\\circ < x < 180^\\circ$):\n$$\\text{Principal angle: } 2x = \\arcsin(0.6) \\approx 36.87^\\circ \\implies x = \\frac{36.87^\\circ}{2} \\approx 18.4^\\circ$$\n$$\\text{Second quadrant: } 2x = 180^\\circ - 36.87^\\circ = 143.13^\\circ \\implies x = \\frac{143.13^\\circ}{2} \\approx 71.6^\\circ$$",
        "State the final solutions:\n$$x = 18.4^\\circ, \\quad 71.6^\\circ$$"
      ],
